And not the normal kind of curse that can be fixed with holy water, or
prayer, or a casting/scroll of remove curse. This is special cursing.

My latest character is a Samurai. The usual mix of ups and downs (seperated
from pet like 3 times by trap doors, which foiled the protection run, BoH
in Minetown, and another in Sokoban, bones file of a Valkyrie who only had
the starting sword and shield...but the shield provided nice defense even
while cursed), until I reached DL 17, where the curse manifested itself
again.

My curse? I keep running into bones files of failed pudding farms.

Seriously, how hard is it to not die on a pudding farm? This one was really
well set up, too. A pathed boulder fortress between the up and down stairs,
an altar right near the down stars, triple engraved Elbereth under each of
about 25 boulders, scroll of scare monster placed adjacent to the altar so
nothing on the altar attacks while you murder them and sac the bodies, rest
of the level completely hollowed out...and yet I found the body of this
person on the other side of the room away from the safe area. Turns out
this was a double bones file, cause I killed one person's ghost, and found
the grave of another person (oddly, I found the gear left by the ghost, but
no tombstone).

Whoever was doing it had been doing it a while. In the various stashes on
the level I found Magicbane, Frostbrand, Werebane, Trollsmasher,
Dragonbane, Demonbane. With the Fire Brand and Snickersnee I had previously
gotten, and the Grayswandir and Sunsword I picked up saccing the puddings
as I cleared the level, I've almost entirely run out of artifacts to
possibly get in the game.

I suppose I shouldn't complain, cause failed pudding farms often do wonders
for my equipment situation (this one had a +3 CoMR, +5 speed boots, 2 pairs
of gauntlets of power, +1 gauntlets of dex, and a helm of brilliance), but
it's really tedious to chop through those endless waves of black jello.

Maybe this was an attempt to seed a bones for another character, but this
seems like a really convoluted way to go about it.


